{
  "case_id": "2021-19-896",
  "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1231(a)(6) states that certain categories of non-citizens, including inadmissible non-citizens like Respondent here, \"may be detained beyond the removal period.\" The question presented in this case is whether that language requires that non-citizens detained under Section 1231(a)(6) be afforded a bond hearing before an immigration judge after six months of detention, at which the government bears the burden of proving by clear and convincing evidence that the non-citizen is either a flight risk or a danger to the community."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent implicitly recognizes the absence of any textual support for his position on the question presented. He accordingly focuses on an altogether different issue, namely, whether he is entitled to outright release under this Court's decision in Zadvydas because his removal is not reasonably foreseeable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Has he actually\nobtained withholding relief? Because there would be a distinction, right, between --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, before he obtains\nthat, you can -- you can keep him in\njail for 50 years? Is that your -- your -- your"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, Justice Breyer. The\ngeneral rule under Demore is that we can keep\nhim in detention pending his proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Was -- was Demore, Mr.\nRaynor -- and I might be wrong about this. Was Demore the one where the Solicitor General\nprovided wrong information to the Court and,\nbasically, the Court was operating on a false\nunderstanding of how long some of these\ndetentions lasted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then, even if you look at the\nentire category of non-citizens, some who\nappeal, some who do not, still the average\nlength of detention is 157 days. And both of\nthose numbers are well below the six months\nthat Zadvydas found presumptively reasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One question --\nwell, a question, counsel. You said that the\nnext hearing in this case, in this particular\nPetitioner's case, was scheduled for 2023.\nBut earlier you said that the average\ndetention rate is below the six months. But\nthat's not true. Average means that it's true\nfor a lot of people, but it's not true for\na lot of people as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent thinks an individual hearing is very\nimportant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shah",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1231(a)(6), as definitively\nconstrued in Zadvydas, forecloses his unchecked\nprolonged detention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Well, can I ask you a question about that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0002-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government has that data. It hasn't disclosed it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: How are you defining \"reasonably foreseeable future\" and on what are you basing that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: What is the status of your client? Has he, in fact, received a bond hearing and is he, in fact, at liberty currently?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He did receive a bond hearing. He was released. The government never appealed his release, by the way, and so he has been free under supervised conditions of release since that time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Shah, would you prevail had Zadvydas not been decided?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shah",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAH: Your Honor, if this Court -- if Zadvydas had not been decided, I think we would need the Court to embrace the same holding that Zadvydas did reach in order for us to prevail at least under our logically antecedent argument. It's built directly upon this Court's holding in Zadvydas."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shah",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAH: Yes, Your Honor. If this Court were to overrule Zadvydas, we lose. But, of course, the government has not asked this Court to overrule Zadvydas. It has asked this Court to apply it just as we do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF AUSTIN RAYNOR ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RAYNOR: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. I'd like to begin just by focusing on the two different arguments in this case. The argument on which we sought certiorari and which the lower court ruled on was the argument that, after six months of detention, a non-citizen is entitled to a bond hearing at which he can prove that he's not a flight --or at which the government has to prove that he's not a flight risk -- or that he is a flight risk or a danger to the community."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a narrower argument. It is specific to non-citizens in withholding-only proceedings. And it would not allow this Court to decide the broader question that it granted cert on and that we sought cert on about the Third Circuit's ruling that all non-citizens covered by Section 1231 are entitled to a bond hearing. Setting aside the fact that it is procedurally barred, it's also incorrect on the merits. Removal here is reasonably foreseeable because this is detention pending proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Lastly, I just want to speak briefly about Demore. Respondent suggested that Demore is not on point because it dealt with criminal non-citizens, and Congress had before it findings about criminal non-citizens. But, here, I think it's important to remember that Congress also had good reasons for treating this category of non-citizens differently, just as, in Demore, Congress had good reasons for treating those non-citizens differently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I ask one question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:06 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Raynor",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d018fbc8512d-0003-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we submit that the Court should do the same thing here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-19-896",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "d018fbc8512df656af15d2d953cd3261bcf7c582a1d96e74b8e5b920601bc3ae",
